{
  "project": {
    "name": "Faircap Water Filter",
    "slug": "faircap-filter",
    "version": "2.1.0",
    "engine": "cadquery",
    "description": {
      "en": "Open-source, print-at-home water filter that screws onto a standard PET bottle neck (PCO-1881) and houses a filter medium — activated charcoal, a hollow-fiber membrane, or a ceramic disc. Screw the cap onto a bottle of raw water, invert, and drink filtered water from the nozzle. Clean water from plastic waste, no commercial dependency.\n\nOfficial Visualizer and Configurator: Yantra4D",
      "es": "Filtro de agua de código abierto e imprimible en casa que se enrosca en el cuello de una botella PET estándar (PCO-1881) y aloja un medio filtrante — carbón activado, membrana de fibra hueca o disco cerámico. Enrosca la tapa en una botella con agua cruda, inviértela y bebe agua filtrada por la boquilla. Agua limpia a partir de residuos plásticos, sin dependencia comercial.\n\nVisualizador y configurador oficial: Yantra4D"
    },
    "thumbnail": "/projects/faircap-filter.png",
    "difficulty": "advanced",
    "tags": [
      "water",
      "filter",
      "humanitarian",
      "upcycling",
      "bottle",
      "pco-1881",
      "hyperobject",
      "commons",
      "cdg"
    ],
